{
  "format": "optibench-workstation",
  "version": 1,
  "meta": {
    "appVersion": "0.1.0-alpha",
    "author": "Optibench examples",
    "created": "2026-11-19T00:00:00.000Z",
    "description": "Showpiece co-simulation. TRANSMITTER: a function generator (2 Hz square wave, 0-5 V) drives a 650 nm laser diode through 100 ohm; above its 20 mA threshold the diode emits ~0.8 W/A x (I - 20 mA), and an EMITTER link makes that optical power the power of the bench laser. OPTICS: the beam is folded by a two-mirror periscope and focused by an f = 50 mm lens onto a 5 mm photodiode head. A DETECTOR link feeds the detected power into the circuit photodiode (0.5 A/W). RECEIVER: the reverse-biased photodiode sources its photocurrent into a 1.5 k transimpedance resistor (RX node ~3-4 V when lit); an NPN switch lights the RX LED, and the RX node clocks a decade counter whose BCD output is decoded onto a 7-segment display that counts received light pulses. Probes TX and RX show both ends of the link. Block the beam (move a mirror) and the counting stops.",
    "dimension": "2d",
    "modified": "2026-11-19T00:00:00.000Z",
    "title": "Free-Space Optical Link"
  },
